# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: Other | Scene: WanderingTheCamp

translate es strings:

    old "Sarah woke up. Outside, she could hear the camp had already come alive."
    new "Sarah se despertó. Fuera, podía oír que el campamento ya había cobrado vida."

    old "Nobody else was left, Ephraim and Caleb had already started their day. Alone again."
    new "No quedaba nadie más, Ephraim y Caleb ya habían comenzado su día. Solos de nuevo."

    old "Sarah began to think about last night. Watching Caleb and Ephraim fuck had been unexpected. So too had been her reaction."
    new "Sarah comenzó a pensar en la noche anterior. Ver a Caleb y a Ephraim follando había sido inesperado. Lo mismo que su reacción."

    old "She could feel herself growing hotter, just remembering."
    new "Podía sentir que se calentaba, solo con recordarlo."

    old "Sarah shook her head. She needed to focus, she couldn't lay in bed masturbating all day."
    new "Sarah negó con la cabeza. Necesitaba concentrarse; no podía estar acostada en la cama masturbándose todo el día."

    old "Sarah stretched her arms. This was not the kind of bed she was used to."
    new "Sarah extendió los brazos. No era la clase de cama a la que estaba acostumbrada."

    old "Sarah got out of bed and began to get dressed."
    new "Sarah se levantó de la cama y comenzó a vestirse."

    old "With most of her clothes lost because of Kate, she was forced to keep wearing the same dress."
    new "Con la mayor parte de sus prendas perdidas por culpa de Kate, se vio obligada a seguir usando el mismo vestido."

    old "Kate..."
    new "Kate..."

    old "Sarah still had trouble to reconcile the Kate she thought she knew, versus what Kate had done to her."
    new "Sarah aún tenía dificultad para conciliar la Kate que creía conocer con lo que Kate había hecho con ella."

    old "Sarah left the tent. The ambiance of the mercenary camp washed over her. It's smells, sounds, the structured chaos."
    new "Sarah salió de la tienda. La atmósfera del campamento mercenario la envolvió: sus olores, sus sonidos, ese caos estructurado."

    old "So different from the castle in which she grew up."
    new "Tan diferente del castillo en el que creció."

    old "Sarah knew this world was different. There were different rules. She had to be careful. Unlike back home, her station offered her little protection."
    new "Sarah sabía que este mundo era diferente. Había reglas distintas. Tenía que tener cuidado. A diferencia de su hogar, su posición le ofrecía poca protección."

    old "Quite the opposite, she realized, if people knew she was a princess, who knew what they would do..."
    new "Al contrario, se dio cuenta, si la gente supiera que era una princesa, ¿quién sabía qué harían..."

    old "Sarah had made her plan, she would go to the harbor and ask around. See if there was a ship heading back to Rosanna."
    new "Sarah había elaborado su plan: iría al puerto, preguntaría por todos lados y vería si había un barco que regresara a Rosanna."

    old "She knew it wasn't much of a plan, but then again, right now, she didn't have many options."
    new "Sabía que no era un gran plan, pero, al fin y al cabo, en ese momento, no tenía muchas opciones."

    old "Walking through the camp, heading to the exit, Sarah was lost in thought."
    new "Caminando por el campamento hacia la salida, Sarah estaba sumida en sus pensamientos."

    old "She suddenly felt a sharp pang against her shin, followed by her losing her balance."
    new "De repente, sintió un golpe agudo en la pantorrilla, seguido de perder el equilibrio."

    old "As Sarah tumbled across the floor, getting dust in her eyes and on her dress, she heard the noise of metal clattering."
    new "Mientras Sarah rodaba por el suelo, ensuciándose los ojos y el vestido con polvo, escuchó el ruido de metal que caía."

    old "She looked up, trying to see what had happened."
    new "Miró hacia arriba, tratando de ver qué había ocurrido."

    old "Instead, she felt herself getting pulled up to her feet with a force stronger than any she had never experienced in her life."
    new "En cambio, sintió que la levantaban con una fuerza más fuerte de la que jamás había sentido en su vida."

    old "She felt the titanic power of the hand, clenched around her upper arm, holding her up."
    new "Sintió la titánica fuerza de la mano, apretada alrededor de su brazo superior, sosteniéndola erguida."

    old "Inches away from her face, she saw the orc's furious gaze."
    new "A pulgadas de su rostro, vio la mirada furiosa del orco."

    old "Look what you've done, you stupid girl!"
    new "¡Mira lo que has hecho, estúpida niña!"

    old "The orc barked at her."
    new "El orco rugió a ella."

    old "Sarah saw, on the ground behind the orc, a plate and some cooking utensils."
    new "Sarah vio, en el suelo detrás del orco, una placa y algunos utensilios de cocina."

    old "She began to realize that, lost in thought, she had knocked over the orc's table, spilling his food onto the floor."
    new "Comenzó a darse cuenta de que, perdida en sus pensamientos, había derribado la mesa del orco, derramando su comida sobre el suelo."

    old "I'm so sorry..."
    new "Lo siento tanto..."

    old "Her voice was weak, the orc radiated a menace that she had never experienced before. She truly believed he might kill her over it."
    new "Su voz era débil; el orco irradiaba una amenaza que ella nunca había experimentado antes. De verdad creía que podría matarla por eso."

    old "Sarah slipped from his grasp and crawled across the floor. She hastily began collecting the plate and everything else she had knocked over."
    new "Sarah se escapó de su agarre y arrastró los restos por el suelo. Con prisas, comenzó a recoger el plato y todo lo demás que había derribado."

    old "She hurried to put it all back on the table. She kept apologizing as she did, hoping the orc would spare her."
    new "Sarah se apresuró a volver a colocar todo sobre la mesa. Seguía disculpándose mientras lo hacía, esperando que el orco la perdonara."

    old "Sarah watched as the orc fell back in his chair, next to his table."
    new "Sarah observó cómo el orco se desplomó en su silla, junto a su mesa."

    old "She watched him, his eyes still full of anger, but seemingly less than before."
    new "La observó, sus ojos aún llenos de furia, pero aparentemente menos que antes."

    old "His arms were like logs, even his legs were large and muscular."
    new "Sus brazos eran como troncos, incluso sus piernas eran grandes y musculosas."

    old "The orc waved his hands, dismissing her without looking at Sarah."
    new "El orco movió las manos, desechándola sin mirar a Sarah."

    old "Go, the damage is already done!"
    new "¡Vete, el daño ya está hecho!"

    old "But gods help you girl if you do something like this again!"
    new "¡Pero los dioses te ayuden si vuelves a hacer algo así, niña!"

    old "Sarah, grasped at her new lease on life and leapt up to her feet."
    new "Sarah, agarró su nueva oportunidad de vida y saltó de pie."

    old "She bowed to the orc, apologizing, as she simultaneously backed away."
    new "Se inclinó ante el orco, disculpándose, mientras retrocedía simultáneamente."

    old "I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry."
    new "Lo siento, lo siento, lo siento."

    old "Get away, she thought, just keep walking. He's letting you live."
    new "Alejate, pensó, sigue caminando. Te deja vivir."

    old "Sarah turned the corner and leaned against the wall, breathing heavily."
    new "Sarah dobló la esquina y se apoyó contra la pared, respirando con dificultad."

    old "A moment of inattention, and she had almost paid for it dearly."
    new "Un momento de distracción y casi había pagado por ello con cara de culo."

    old "She had to get out of here."
    new "Tenía que salir de aquí."

    old "Sarah made her way to the camp's gate, marching as fast as she could."
    new "Sarah se dirigió a la puerta del campamento, marchando lo más rápido que podía."

    old "After this, down the road, past the shops, into the harbor. She tried to remember the path that Kate had dragged her along."
    new "Después de esto, por el camino, más allá de las tiendas, hacia el puerto. Intentó recordar el sendero que Kate la había arrastrado a seguir."

    old "A man blocked her path."
    new "Un hombre bloqueó su camino."

    old "Hold on there."
    new "Espera un momento."

    old "The man was large, easily blocking Sarah from getting past him. He pushed her back."
    new "El hombre era enorme, bloqueando fácilmente el paso de Sarah. La empujó hacia atrás."

    old "I need to leave, I have to get to the harbor."
    new "Necesito marcharme, tengo que llegar al puerto."

    old "The camp guard shook his head."
    new "El guardia del campamento negó con la cabeza."

    old "You're not going anywhere. Orders, straight from Vaelen himself."
    new "No te mueves de aquí. Órdenes directas del propio Vaelen."

    old "Sarah was stunned."
    new "Sarah estaba atónita."

    old "You don't even know who I am, just let me go, please."
    new "Ni siquiera sabes quién soy, déjame ir, por favor."

    old "She pleaded with the guard."
    new "Sarah suplicó al guardia."

    old "The guard shook his head again. He planted his feet firmer, as if to reinforce his point."
    new "El guardia negó con la cabeza de nuevo. Afianzó los pies con más firmeza, como si quisiera reforzar su punto."

    old "Vaelen told me himself, keep the blonde girl in the pretty dress from leaving."
    new "¡Vaelen me lo dijo él mismo: evita que la rubia del vestido precioso se vaya!"

    old "It might surprise you to learn, but there aren't a lot of people here matching that description."
    new "Te sorprendería saberlo, pero no hay muchos aquí que encajen con esa descripción."

    old "Sarah thought about what she could do, but there was no way she was getting past the guard."
    new "Sarah pensó en qué podía hacer, pero no había forma de pasar al guardia."

    old "She turned around and began to walk back into the camp."
    new "Sarah dio la vuelta y comenzó a caminar de regreso al campamento."

    old "Sarah had lost the speed in her step. There was nowhere for her to walk to, other then back to the tent."
    new "Sarah había perdido el brío en su andar. No había lugar al que caminar, salvo volver a la tienda."

    old "She went back the way she came."
    new "Volvió por el camino que había seguido."

    old "She passed the orc, and quickly glanced in his direction."
    new "Ella pasó al orco y echó un vistazo rápido en su dirección."

    old "The orc met her eyes."
    new "El orco la miró a los ojos."

    old "Sarah turned her eyes back to the ground, hoping to avoid his wrath a second time."
    new "Sarah volvió la mirada al suelo, esperando evitar su ira por segunda vez."

    old "She took a wide berth around his table."
    new "Se apartó mucho de su mesa."

    old "Sarah eventually made her way back to the tent."
    new "Sarah finalmente hizo su camino de vuelta a la tienda."

    old "To her surprise, the flap to the tent was thrown aside, and Kate came storming out."
    new "Para su sorpresa, la entrada de la tienda fue arrojada hacia un lado y Kate salió corriendo."

    old "Sarah! Are you ok? I heard about you and Atilla..."
    new "¡Sarah! ¿Estás bien? He oído hablar de ti y de Atilla..."

    old "Sarah looked confused, for a moment forgetting what had transpired between them."
    new "Sarah se veía confundida, olvidando por un momento lo que había ocurrido entre ellos."

    old "Atilla?"
    new "¿Atilla?"

    old "The orc, that vile creature. Did he hurt you?"
    new "El orco, esa bestia abominable. ¿Te hizo daño?"

    old "Sarah felt her upper arm. It was bruised, but other than that, she was more scared than hurt."
    new "Sarah tocó su hombro. Estaba morado, pero más allá de eso, tenía más miedo que dolor."

    old "Kate embraced Sarah."
    new "Kate abrazó a Sarah."

    old "Thank the gods, I was so worried that he would hurt you."
    new "Gracias a los dioses, estaba tan preocupada de que te hiciera daño."

    old "Sarah suddenly pushed Kate away."
    new "Sarah empujó a Kate con un jadeo de pánico repentino."

    old "Only one person in this camp has hurt me..."
    new "Solo una persona en este campamento me ha hecho daño..."

    old "Sarah stared daggers at Kate."
    new "Sarah clavó la mirada en Kate con furia de puñal."

    old "Kate looked away in shame."
    new "Kate desvió la mirada con vergüenza."

    old "I know..."
    new "Lo sé..."

    old "Usually, Kate's voice was strong, but now, it was soft and weak."
    new "Normalmente, la voz de Kate era fuerte, pero ahora sonaba suave y débil."

    old "What I did to you, Sarah..."
    new "Lo que hice contigo, Sarah..."

    old "Why did you do it, Kate? I thought we were friends."
    new "¿Por qué lo hiciste, Kate? Pensaba que éramos amigas."

    old "When you made love to me, after the funeral...did it mean nothing to you?"
    new "¿Cuando te hiciste el amor conmigo después del funeral... significaba nada para ti?"

    old "Kate sagged down, sitting down by the entrance to the tent."
    new "Kate se dejó caer, sentándose junto a la entrada de la tienda."

    old "Sarah...will you let me explain?"
    new "Sarah... ¿me dejarás explicarte?"

    old "I want to know why you did it."
    new "Quiero saber por qué lo hiciste."

    old "Sarah fights every urge to tell Kate to leave, and nods."
    new "Sarah lucha contra cada impulso de decirle a Kate que se vaya y asiente."

    old "The two old friends go into the tent together."
    new "Los dos viejos amigos entraron juntos en la tienda."

    old "They sit down together on the same bed."
    new "Se sientan juntos en la misma cama."

    old "They're quiet for a long time. Kate finally breaks the silence."
    new "Callan en silencio durante un largo tiempo. Kate rompe finalmente el silencio."

    old "I've tried to be honest with you, Sarah. As honest as I could be."
    new "He tratado de ser honesta contigo, Sarah. Tan honesta como pude."

    old "But when I told you about my life after running away, there were a lot of things I didn't tell you about."
    new "Pero cuando te conté sobre mi vida después de huir, hubo muchas cosas que no te dije."

    old "Kate pulls her knees to her chest."
    new "Kate aprieta sus rodillas contra su pecho."

    old "This world...it can be very cruel to a girl, all alone."
    new "Este mundo... puede ser muy cruel para una niña, sola."

    old "To survive, I had to do a lot of things that...I didn't want to tell you about."
    new "Para sobrevivir, tuve que hacer muchas cosas de las que... no quiero contarte."

    old "For a long time, my life was pretty miserable. Everywhere I went, I was alone. People would be so cruel to me..."
    new "Por un largo tiempo, mi vida fue bastante miserable. A donde fuera, estaba sola. La gente era tan cruel conmigo..."

    old "Sarah noticed Kate turning more quiet, more inward."
    new "Sarah notó que Kate se volvía más callada, más introspectiva."

    old "Sarah surprised herself when she found her own hand, moving across her friend's back, comforting her."
    new "Sarah se sorprendió a sí misma cuando encontró su propia mano moviéndose por la espalda de su amiga, consolándola."

    old "Why do I still love her, Sarah thought to herself. She felt her hatred for Kate slip out of her fingers."
    new "¿Por qué todavía la amo, pensó Sarah para sí misma. Sintió cómo su odio por Kate se le escapaba entre los dedos."

    old "I tried to be strong, but some days...the pain was just too much."
    new "Intenté ser fuerte, pero algunos días... el dolor simplemente era demasiado."

    old "I developed ways of dealing with that pain..."
    new "Encontré formas de lidiar con ese dolor..."

    old "There were a few things, like drugs, but above all, alcohol."
    new "Había algunas cosas, como las drogas, pero sobre todo, el alcohol."

    old "Kate paused again, staring off into a memory that Sarah could not reach."
    new "Kate se detuvo otra vez, mirando hacia el recuerdo al que Sarah no podía acceder."

    old "It numbed the pain, and it let me survive when things got too bad. But over time, the cure got worse than the disease."
    new "Adormeció el dolor y me permitió sobrevivir cuando las cosas se ponían demasiado mal. Pero con el tiempo, la cura se volvió peor que la enfermedad."

    old "I found myself blacked out in alleys, no idea how I got there."
    new "Me encontré inconsciente en callejones, sin idea de cómo llegué allí."

    old "Kate stared at Sarah, tears were running down Kate's face."
    new "Kate miró a Sarah y las lágrimas corrían por su rostro."

    old "I was going to die there, Sarah, I knew it in my heart back then. One day I would black out in some alley, and someone would cut my throat or I would freeze to death, I just knew it."
    new "Voy a morir allí, Sarah, lo sabía con todo mi corazón en ese entonces. Un día me desmayaría en algún callejón y alguien me cortaría la garganta o me congelaría hasta morir, simplemente lo sabía."

    old "And this world would throw me away like garbage."
    new "Y este mundo me tiraría a la basura como si fuera un desecho."

    old "Sarah embraced her friend, who had now opened up to her."
    new "Sarah abrazó a su amiga, quien ahora se había abierto con ella."

    old "That's when they found me, when Vaelen found me. They pulled me from the void and they gave me a life. A life I always wanted."
    new "Fue entonces cuando me encontraron, cuando Vaelen me encontró. Me sacaron del vacío y me dieron una vida. Una vida que siempre quise."

    old "But those old wounds...they never fully healed. This disease, the addiction, it's inside of me in a way I can't explain."
    new "Pero esas viejas heridas... nunca sanaron por completo. Esta enfermedad, la adicción, están dentro de mí de una manera que no puedo explicar."

    old "What you saw, what I did to you...that's not who I am...or...who I want to be...I mean."
    new "Lo que viste, lo que hice contigo... eso no es quién soy yo... o... quién quiero ser... digo."

    old "Sarah reached out. She clasped Kate's head between her hands."
    new "Sarah se estiró y sujetó la cabeza de Kate entre sus manos."

    old "Sarah didn't know why, only that she needed to. She leaned in and kissed Kate."
    new "Sarah no sabía por qué, solo que necesitaba hacerlo. Se inclinó y besó a Kate."

    old "Kate seemed as stunned as Sarah."
    new "Kate parecía tan atónita como Sarah."

    old "Ooh, Kate..."
    new "Oh, Kate..."

    old "Tears kept streaming down Kate's face."
    new "Las lágrimas seguían deslizándose por el rostro de Kate."

    old "Sarah, I'm so sorry."
    new "Sarah, lo siento tanto."

    old "She was sobbing by now."
    new "Ya lloraba."

    old "Sarah pulled Kate into a tight embrace, and together the friends fell back into the bed."
    new "Sarah tiró de Kate hacia un abrazo apretado y, juntas, las amigas cayeron de nuevo sobre la cama."

    old "For what felt like hours, the two remained in a silent embrace, healing wounds of betrayal without speaking."
    new "Por lo que parecieron horas, los dos permanecieron en un abrazo silencioso, sanando las heridas de la traición sin hablar."

    old "Sharing pain, without words."
    new "Compartiendo el dolor, sin palabras."

    old "In the end, Kate got back up to her feet."
    new "Al final, Kate se puso de pie."

    old "I know I don't deserve it, but I hope I can earn your forgiveness one day."
    new "Lo sé, no lo merezco, pero espero poder ganarme tu perdón algún día."

    old "Sarah looked up at her friend."
    new "Sarah miró a su amiga."

    old "There is nothing left to forgive."
    new "No queda nada que perdonar."

    old "Kate bowed her head low."
    new "Kate inclinó la cabeza con sumisión."

    old "I've spoken to Vaelen about you. We're going to see what we can do. Maybe get you back safe to Rosanna."
    new "He hablado con Vaelen sobre ti. Vamos a ver qué podemos hacer. Quizás logremos llevarte de vuelta a Rosanna a salvo."

    old "Kate turns and quickly leaves the tent, hiding her face as she runs off into the camp."
    new "Kate da la vuelta y sale rápidamente de la tienda, ocultando el rostro mientras se aleja corriendo por el campamento."

    old "There is nothing to explain, leave me alone."
    new "No hay nada que explicar, déjame en paz."

    old "Kate gets up and walks away. She can't bring herself to face Sarah."
    new "Kate se levanta y se aleja. No puede enfrentarse a Sarah."

    old "Vaelen wants to speak to you."
    new "Vaelen quiere hablar contigo."

    old "It's the last thing Kate says before she storms off."
    new "Es lo último que Kate dice antes de irse enfadada."

    old "Sarah goes into the tent and falls down onto the bed."
    new "Sarah entra en la tienda y se deja caer sobre la cama."

    old "It's still day, but she can't bring herself to get out of the bed anymore."
    new "Aún es de día, pero no puede sacarse de la cama."
